35,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The ledger shows our allocation is down a quarter, and home visits earn no tariff. We must build on-site to recover costs.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, on-site billing is a trap. The booking system only logs fixed slots. If we can’t record the work, it vanishes from every report.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, that’s a valid concern. But my staffing data shows therapy is hemorrhaging staff, while midwifery has unexpected slack. We must balance the load carefully.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Shion, you’re right. If it isn’t booked, it doesn’t exist. But the rooms are full by mid-morning. Where do we even put the next patient?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, that slack in midwifery is a blessing. But I found our shared clinic collapsed when no one owned the rota. We must ensure clear ownership this time.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, clear ownership is vital. But with the budget cut and no tariff for home visits, we must prioritize on-site care that actually generates revenue.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, revenue is a distraction. The trial proved the model works, but the system erases it. We need a program that fits the existing slots, or it’s just another ghost.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, I agree the system is flawed, but we can’t ignore the human cost. With nine nursing posts empty, adding more on-site pressure risks breaking the ward entirely.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, nine empty posts is terrifying. But if we pick a program that needs no new rooms, we might save the day. Can we fit it into the existing schedule?","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, I worry about the physical barriers. Our shared round lost a third of visits to locked gates and weather. We must plan for the real world, not just the schedule.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, you’re right that unrecorded work vanishes. But on-site sessions bill at standard rates. We need a program that fits existing slots to generate the revenue we desperately need.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, you’re chasing revenue while ignoring the data. The trial worked, but the system erased it. We need a model that survives the booking screen, not just the ledger.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Kenji, the therapy team is shrinking, so a new unit is impossible. But midwifery has slack. Could we use that capacity for a perinatal service?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, that’s clever! If midwifery has slack, we avoid new rooms. But can we book those classes in the system? I need to know if they’ll actually show up.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, that slack is precious. But remember, our shared clinic failed because no one owned the rota. We must name a single leader before we begin.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, using midwifery slack is smart. But with the budget cut, we must ensure this on-site service bills at standard rates to cover its own running costs.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Midori, if the perinatal service uses fixed slots, it survives the system. But if it relies on ad-hoc follow-ups, it becomes invisible. We need structure, not just goodwill.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, you’re right about structure. But @Shizue, I worry about the joint ownership. If midwifery and pediatrics don’t agree on the rota, we repeat the clinic’s failure.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, I’m glad we found a path that doesn’t need new rooms! But @Shion, if the classes aren’t booked as fixed slots, they’ll vanish from the records. We must ensure every session is logged properly.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Midori"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, you are right. I have seen the rota fail when ownership is shared. We must name one person to hold the line, or it will crumble again.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
